WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.440
Is The Oracle’s guardian Seraph&nbsp;
an angel? Were Kid and Commander&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.440 --> 00:00:08.720
Locke both casualties of war following The&nbsp;
Matrix Revolutions? How did the Analyst rise&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:12.880
to power? These are all questions that&nbsp;
could be answered in future spin-offs.

00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:18.800
Though Trinity is killed at the end of the third&nbsp;
Matrix movie, she and Neo get a new chance at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:23.920
life in The Matrix Resurrections, as it's later&nbsp;
revealed that the machines resurrected both of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:29.200
them in order to support the Analyst's version of&nbsp;
the Matrix. Furthermore, Trinity goes through a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:34.400
major development in the film when she learns&nbsp;
that she, too, now has the powers of the One.

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:39.200
While the first Matrix does provide some&nbsp;
clues to Trinity's past — explaining that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:44.320
she was once a master hacker — not much else&nbsp;
has been revealed about her early days. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:49.520
a prequel could do a lot to fill in those&nbsp;
blanks. Carrie-Anne Moss has even teased&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:53.280
some of her own ideas about Trinity's&nbsp;
origins in interviews. For example,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:57.840
she told GQ that she believes the character&nbsp;
was freed from the Matrix at an early age.

00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:01.840
Trinity's greatest hacking triumphs&nbsp;
could be depicted in this spin-off,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:06.160
along with her many encounters with&nbsp;
Agent Smith who, in Revolutions,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.160 --> 00:01:11.280
claims to have failed in capturing her more than&nbsp;
any other human. Alternately, while it's almost&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:16.240
a certainty that Trinity would be the co-star&nbsp;
of any potential follow-ups to Resurrections,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:19.760
that doesn't mean she couldn't star&nbsp;
in a solo sequel adventure, too.

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:25.200
Originally portrayed by Laurence Fishburne,&nbsp;
Morpheus is a character who captures viewers'&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:29.680
attention every time he's on-screen —&nbsp;
and often when he's not. The captain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.680 --> 00:01:34.880
of the Nebuchadnezzar is everything&nbsp;
you'd want from a leader: wise, warm,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.880 --> 00:01:42.160
strong, and never without hope. Without Morpheus'&nbsp;
faith in the One, Neo might never have been freed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.160 --> 00:01:47.280
from the Matrix. And it's that same belief&nbsp;
that prevents further bloodshed in Zion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:53.040
after he realizes Neo and the Machines have&nbsp;
allied against Agent Smith. That same faith,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:57.760
however, can also be somewhat of an Achilles'&nbsp;
heel for Morpheus; in The Matrix Resurrections,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.760 --> 00:02:02.480
Niobe explains that it caused him to&nbsp;
underestimate the looming threat of the Analyst.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.480 --> 00:02:07.520
While Resurrections suggests Morpheus was a&nbsp;
casualty of the ensuing machine attack, that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.520 --> 00:02:12.960
movie sees Neo create a youthful, A.I. version&nbsp;
of his mentor, played by Yahya Abdul-Mateen II.

00:02:13.840 --> 00:02:14.480
"At last…"

00:02:16.240 --> 00:02:21.680
The great thing about a possible Morpheus spin-off&nbsp;
is that there's already a fair amount of backstory&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:26.400
to work with. Elements from his past mentioned&nbsp;
in the Matrix comics could be expanded upon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:29.280
along with the beginning of his&nbsp;
relationship and falling out with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:33.360
Niobe — not to mention his time as High&nbsp;
Chair of the Zion Council. Similarly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:38.800
the origins of Abdul-Mateen's half-Morpheus,&nbsp;
half-Smith replica could also be explored.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:44.720
And a post-Resurrections spin-off starring that&nbsp;
version of Morpheus has a lot of promise, too.

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:50.720
Niobe is one of the undeniable standout&nbsp;
characters of the Matrix sequels,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.720 --> 00:02:55.120
and one of the patron saints of Matrix&nbsp;
spin-offs thanks to her star turn in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.120 --> 00:03:00.960
2003 video game Enter the Matrix. A fearless&nbsp;
leader with a calm yet commanding presence,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.960 --> 00:03:05.440
she remains by far one of the best&nbsp;
contenders for a Matrix spin-off.

00:03:05.440 --> 00:03:09.920
Being the only character from the original&nbsp;
resistance to appear in The Matrix Resurrections&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.920 --> 00:03:15.440
other than Trinity and Neo, Niobe has a wealth of&nbsp;
story possibilities worth exploring. A spin-off&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.440 --> 00:03:20.320
starring the character could explore her early&nbsp;
days in Zion or the original Matrix. Or, it could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.320 --> 00:03:25.520
reveal in detail the events that occurred between&nbsp;
Revolutions and Resurrections. More specifically,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.520 --> 00:03:31.840
it might focus on the formation of IO — Zion's&nbsp;
successor — and Niobe's rise to become its leader.

00:03:32.480 --> 00:03:37.600
True to his name, Ghost doesn't appear as often&nbsp;
as his captain, Niobe, in the second and third&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.600 --> 00:03:43.360
Matrix movies. But he gets an enormous amount of&nbsp;
screen-time in Enter the Matrix, in which he and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.360 --> 00:03:49.040
Niobe are the two playable characters. An avid&nbsp;
student of philosophy with a wry sense of humor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:55.280
and an otherwise no-nonsense demeanor, Ghost would&nbsp;
be a great candidate for more Matrix spin-offs.

00:03:55.280 --> 00:04:01.040
A prequel series to the original trilogy could&nbsp;
show how Ghost ends up joining Niobe on the Logos&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:06.880
and how he becomes such an expert shot, as well&nbsp;
as the origins of his unrequited crush on Trinity.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.880 --> 00:04:11.040
Conversely, a spin-off set after the first&nbsp;
three films could reveal what happened to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.040 --> 00:04:16.160
him in the more than 60-year gap before&nbsp;
Resurrections, including how he handles&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.160 --> 00:04:22.160
the news of Trinity's demise. Perhaps his heroics&nbsp;
in Revolutions even earn him a ship of his own.

00:04:23.120 --> 00:04:28.560
The Matrix's most notorious Agent,&nbsp;
Smith, proves you can't keep a bad&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.560 --> 00:04:33.360
program down in Resurrections, in which&nbsp;
he's reincarnated in a new identity as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.360 --> 00:04:38.640
Thomas Anderson's boss and business partner.&nbsp;
Smith and Neo's mutual hatred of the Analyst&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.640 --> 00:04:43.360
leads the two to briefly join forces near&nbsp;
the movie's end, and the notorious agent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.360 --> 00:04:47.760
lets his own boss know exactly how he&nbsp;
feels — by filling him with bullets.

00:04:47.760 --> 00:04:51.120
Once Smith has accomplished his&nbsp;
objective, he leaves Neo and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.120 --> 00:04:54.480
Trinity to be hunted down by&nbsp;
the Analyst's legion of bots.

00:04:54.480 --> 00:04:58.320
"You know the difference between&nbsp;
us, Tom? Anyone could have been you.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.360 --> 00:05:00.560
Whereas I've always been anyone."

00:05:01.920 --> 00:05:07.360
This begs the question: Where did he go? A&nbsp;
Smith spin-off could answer that question,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.360 --> 00:05:12.400
showcasing his activities after Resurrections.&nbsp;
Just what plot will he come up with next to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.400 --> 00:05:16.800
fight the Architect and keep his freedom?&nbsp;
Will he be a friend or a foe when Neo and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.800 --> 00:05:20.960
Trinity decide to remake the Matrix, as they&nbsp;
promise to do at the end of Resurrections?

00:05:20.960 --> 00:05:24.400
While future Matrix movies would&nbsp;
likely answer those questions,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.400 --> 00:05:29.360
a spin-off could surely delve further into the&nbsp;
details. Another option would be to explore&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.360 --> 00:05:33.760
Smith's activities in the previous version&nbsp;
of the Matrix from the original trilogy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.760 --> 00:05:39.200
which could allow Hugo Weaving to return to the&nbsp;
role. Better yet, a Smith project could go back&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.200 --> 00:05:44.560
even further in time, revealing whether or not&nbsp;
the earlier iterations of the Matrix included&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.560 --> 00:05:50.240
a version of Smith to balance out their versions&nbsp;
of the One — a subject of much debate among fans.

00:05:51.240 --> 00:05:56.320
Bugs is the captain of the Mnemosyne in The Matrix&nbsp;
Resurrections, as well as the red pill who frees&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:56.320 --> 00:06:02.240
Neo from the Matrix's latest reincarnation.&nbsp;
Brave, good-humored, and not one for following&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.240 --> 00:06:07.040
orders when she feels they're wrong, Bugs would&nbsp;
be a perfect candidate for a Matrix spin-off.

00:06:07.040 --> 00:06:11.840
Given how her Matrix extraction occurs&nbsp;
not long before she does the same for Neo,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:11.840 --> 00:06:17.440
it wouldn't be necessary to de-age the character&nbsp;
digitally for a prequel, provided it focuses on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:17.440 --> 00:06:23.040
Bugs as a young adult. Be it a prequel or sequel,&nbsp;
however, Jessica Henwick could easily slip back&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:23.040 --> 00:06:28.560
into the role, and Resurrections shows that Bugs&nbsp;
is well-known for heading out on solo missions,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:28.560 --> 00:06:33.840
too. That said, the spin-off could also spotlight&nbsp;
her Mnemosyne crewmates to flesh them out further,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:33.840 --> 00:06:37.280
more clearly establishing how each&nbsp;
of them relates with their captain.

00:06:38.240 --> 00:06:44.320
Though purged from the Matrix some time before&nbsp;
Resurrections, the Oracle is far from forgotten.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:44.320 --> 00:06:49.040
Morpheus tells Neo in The Matrix that the Oracle&nbsp;
has sided with Zion since the human rebellion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.040 --> 00:06:55.120
began. However, the Architect reveals in Reloaded&nbsp;
that her existence extends back even further,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:55.120 --> 00:07:00.400
as she helped him create the first successful&nbsp;
version of the machines' simulated reality.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.400 --> 00:07:05.120
Given that there have been seven versions&nbsp;
of the Matrix and the initial two failed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.120 --> 00:07:09.360
the Oracle might have been around&nbsp;
as far back as the third Matrix,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:09.360 --> 00:07:13.280
meaning she has a wealth of&nbsp;
backstory ripe for exploration.

00:07:13.280 --> 00:07:17.280
A prequel spin-off starring the Oracle&nbsp;
could answer many long-standing mysteries,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:17.280 --> 00:07:21.760
such as what the other iterations of the Matrix&nbsp;
were like, how she met her bodyguard Seraph,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:21.760 --> 00:07:27.040
and when she first rebelled against the Architect.&nbsp;
It could also feature Neo's predecessors, since&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:27.040 --> 00:07:32.000
each Matrix the Oracle co-created also&nbsp;
contained its own version of the One.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:32.000 --> 00:07:37.040
The character would likely be recast, as her&nbsp;
original actor, Gloria Foster, passed away,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:37.040 --> 00:07:42.960
while her second actor, Mary Alice, hasn't worked&nbsp;
in entertainment media for some time. Not that a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.960 --> 00:07:47.760
sequel spin-off is out of the question, however.&nbsp;
The Merovingian does explain in Revolutions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:47.760 --> 00:07:52.560
that the Oracle can give her eyes to others.&nbsp;
Could she have passed them on to a successor?

00:07:53.520 --> 00:07:58.080
The Matrix movies have dropped countless hints&nbsp;
about the mysterious program known as Seraph.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:58.080 --> 00:08:02.960
In The Matrix Revolutions, he's referred to as&nbsp;
"wingless" by one of the Merovingian's enforcers.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.960 --> 00:08:08.880
The Merv himself even reveals later on that the&nbsp;
two have a past association. While it's unclear&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:08.880 --> 00:08:14.640
whether Seraph ever actually had wings, this clue,&nbsp;
as well as his white costume and Biblical name,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:14.640 --> 00:08:19.600
suggests he may have at one point been an&nbsp;
angel within the Matrix. This theory is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:19.600 --> 00:08:24.160
further supported when the Merovingian calls&nbsp;
him "the angel without his wings" in French.

00:08:24.160 --> 00:08:28.960
Seraph may even be a Seraphim, who were&nbsp;
once the "Agents" of the paradise Matrix.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.960 --> 00:08:33.440
Interestingly, he almost starred in what&nbsp;
became the Matrix: Path of Neo video game.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:33.440 --> 00:08:38.160
Though that story wasn't to be, it doesn't mean&nbsp;
Seraph can't get another chance at a spin-off.

00:08:38.160 --> 00:08:42.000
In addition to examining his true&nbsp;
nature and past with the Merovingian,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:45.840
the spin-off could uncover why Seraph&nbsp;
is absent from the first Matrix movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:45.840 --> 00:08:50.080
despite the Oracle's claim that he's been her&nbsp;
bodyguard for some time. It could also depict his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:50.080 --> 00:08:54.480
battles with Agent Smith — whom, in Revolutions,&nbsp;
Seraph claims he has defeated in the past.

00:08:55.120 --> 00:08:57.760
"You do not truly know&nbsp;
someone until you fight them."

00:08:58.560 --> 00:09:02.640
Neo is always shown to be uncomfortable&nbsp;
with the hero worship he receives&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:02.640 --> 00:09:06.720
from many of Zion's inhabitants, which&nbsp;
is one of the reasons he finds Kid&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:06.720 --> 00:09:11.840
particularly difficult to be around. Since meeting&nbsp;
Neo on the day he freed himself from the Matrix,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:11.840 --> 00:09:17.200
Kid has idolized humanity's prophesied savior,&nbsp;
and he clearly states his intention to one day&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:17.200 --> 00:09:22.160
serve aboard the Nebuchadnezzar — a prospect&nbsp;
nobody on the ship is too thrilled about. Still,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:22.160 --> 00:09:26.160
he proves to be a pretty remarkable person&nbsp;
himself in Zion's battle against the Machines&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:26.160 --> 00:09:31.280
by helping Captain Mifune reload while fighting&nbsp;
off Sentinels. After a timely save from Zee,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:31.280 --> 00:09:35.040
he also gives the Hammer the&nbsp;
opening it needs to re-enter Zion.

00:09:35.040 --> 00:09:37.280
Kid appears in The Matrix Online afterwards,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:37.280 --> 00:09:42.160
helming a ship fittingly called Neo's Hope.&nbsp;
Oddly, he's not present in Resurrections,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:42.160 --> 00:09:46.720
despite being significantly younger than most of&nbsp;
the major characters in the first three movies.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:46.720 --> 00:09:51.440
It's possible he was one of the many casualties&nbsp;
from the Machines' renewed war on Zion, of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:51.440 --> 00:09:56.240
but nobody can know for sure. A spin-off&nbsp;
could easily tie up this loose end, however,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:56.240 --> 00:10:00.960
and show Kid further coming into&nbsp;
his own as a hero after Revolutions.

00:10:02.000 --> 00:10:07.680
Jason Lock is introduced in The Matrix Reloaded as&nbsp;
Morpheus' opposite. He's a hardened pragmatist who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:07.680 --> 00:10:13.440
neither believes in the One nor has any love lost&nbsp;
for Morpheus — the man who once dated his lover,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:13.440 --> 00:10:18.640
Niobe. Though arguably an effective tactician&nbsp;
and leader of Zion's forces in the real world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:18.640 --> 00:10:22.320
Lock's disdain for Morpheus and his&nbsp;
beliefs often cloud his judgment,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:22.320 --> 00:10:26.560
causing him to repeatedly underestimate Neo's&nbsp;
importance in the war against the Machines.

00:10:26.560 --> 00:10:31.120
Though he becomes an important figure in The&nbsp;
Matrix Online, Lock is not seen in Resurrections,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:31.120 --> 00:10:36.480
suggesting his relationship with Niobe at one&nbsp;
point ended for any number of reasons — perhaps&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:36.480 --> 00:10:41.360
even his demise. A spin-off featuring&nbsp;
him could shed some light on his fate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:41.360 --> 00:10:46.400
and reveal whether or not his contentious&nbsp;
relationship with Morpheus improved after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:46.400 --> 00:10:51.760
Neo saved Zion. It would also be an opportunity&nbsp;
to humanize Lock and make him more sympathetic,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:51.760 --> 00:10:55.920
as he is somewhat of an antagonistic&nbsp;
figure in the original Matrix trilogy.

00:10:57.200 --> 00:11:03.600
Who better to tell the full story of the Matrix&nbsp;
than the two programs who've seen them all? The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:03.600 --> 00:11:08.240
Architect alone created six versions of the&nbsp;
Matrix, aided by the Oracle in the later&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:08.240 --> 00:11:13.280
versions. A spin-off starring him or both&nbsp;
characters could feature every iteration,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:13.280 --> 00:11:19.040
showing how they changed over time. Though the&nbsp;
Architect himself is certainly not an action hero,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:19.040 --> 00:11:23.520
he would have both the Seraphim and the&nbsp;
Agents to back him up on his adventures,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:23.520 --> 00:11:28.960
facing off against the Ones who existed before&nbsp;
Neo. This spin-off could also address whether&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:28.960 --> 00:11:33.040
the Architect himself changed with each&nbsp;
new Matrix iteration. In the original&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:33.040 --> 00:11:36.640
paradise version, for example, could&nbsp;
he have looked or dressed more like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:36.640 --> 00:11:41.360
artistic depictions of the Judeo-Christian&nbsp;
God? Similarly, could the Oracle's appearance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:41.360 --> 00:11:46.560
have resembled that of oracles of classical&nbsp;
antiquity, like those found in Ancient Greece?

00:11:46.560 --> 00:11:51.120
The Analyst, meanwhile, has only created the&nbsp;
seventh Matrix, but that doesn't mean he's not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:51.120 --> 00:11:56.240
worthy of a spin-off of his own. Perhaps such a&nbsp;
film could show how he overthrew the Architect&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:56.240 --> 00:12:00.320
in the first place. This would also provide&nbsp;
a good opportunity to elaborate on events&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:00.320 --> 00:12:05.760
referenced in Resurrections, including his mass&nbsp;
purging of rebellious programs — which might&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:05.760 --> 00:12:11.440
give some much-needed closure for characters&nbsp;
such as the Oracle, Rama Kandra, and Kamala.

